# $k$-Nearest Neighbors

> **Topic:** k-Nearest Neighbors (from scratch), Classification Error, k-Selection, Wine Recommender
> **Dataset:** Wine Dataset


---

## Overview

This notebook builds the **$k$-Nearest Neighbors (KNN)** algorithm entirely from scratch using NumPy and applies it to the Wine dataset. No `sklearn` model classes are used for training — every component (`distance`, `k_nearest_neighbors`, `KNN_predict`, `classification_error`) is implemented directly.

The notebook covers the full KNN workflow: from a from-scratch Euclidean distance function through majority-vote classification, to a sweep over odd values of $k$ to find the optimal neighbourhood size. It also includes a **wine recommender system** — a natural application of KNN that demonstrates how the same algorithm used for classification can be repurposed to answer "given a wine I liked, which other wines are most similar?"

---

